# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Coinpresso agent — environment
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit .env.local.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Uncomment and fill both to run live. Left commented (or left as the placeholder
# text), the app stays in mock mode — which is deliberate, so that copying this
# file does not produce a build that thinks it has keys and fails on a 401
# three minutes into the first run.

# --- MODEL CREDENTIALS: pick ONE of the two modes below --------------------

# DIRECT MODE. Straight to the providers with these keys. On Railway put them in
# project-level SHARED variables so every Pexalo service reads one set rather
# than each carrying its own copy.
#
# Strategy agent (research + web search) and Writer agent.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#
# Review agent (style + compliance enforcement).
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# GATEWAY MODE. This app holds no provider key at all — Pexalo HQ holds them and
# forwards the call, attributing the spend to the client. Set BOTH or NEITHER: a
# URL without a token fails every call with a 401 that looks like a provider
# problem, so the app refuses that combination and stays direct.
# See PEXALO-AI-GATEWAY-SPEC.md for the endpoint contract.
# PEXALO_AI_URL=https://api.pexalo.com
# PEXALO_SERVICE_TOKEN=

# --- STORAGE ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the file-backed stores live. REQUIRED on Railway, where the container
# filesystem is ephemeral and a deploy would otherwise wipe every run, the
# archive, the campaign fact sheets and the saved credentials. Mount a volume
# and point this at it. Left unset locally, it defaults to ./.data
# DATA_DIR=/data

# Model selection. Defaults are set in src/lib/models.ts — override here only
# if you want to move a stage up or down a tier.
# STRATEGY_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# WRITER_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# REVIEWER_MODEL=gpt-5

# Optional. When unset the app runs in MOCK mode: the full pipeline executes
# with canned agent responses so the dashboard is explorable without spend.
# Set to "1" to force mock even when keys are present.
# MOCK_AGENTS=1

# Google export (optional — approval step writes a Doc and updates the calendar).
# Service account JSON, base64-encoded, with Docs + Sheets + Drive scope.
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_B64=
# CONTENT_CALENDAR_SHEET_ID=1WBmkWxbpfeORG_uL8Kl9JAGdYcVjh5qaBA61qstbMmc
# GOOGLE_DRIVE_FOLDER_ID=

# --- Portal login -----------------------------------------------------------
# The app has no user accounts. Two shared passcodes gate it until Pexalo HQ's
# portal fronts it. REQUIRED in production: without either, every page and API
# route returns 503 on purpose. In development, unset means open (admin).
#   PORTAL_PASSCODE        the Coinpresso team (Elena, Liam) — plan, approve, publish
#   PORTAL_ADMIN_PASSCODE  Pexalo — everything above plus the billing figure and
#                          the data-snapshot restore on the Settings page
#   PORTAL_SECRET          optional; signs the session cookie. Defaults to the
#                          passcodes, so rotating a passcode logs everyone out.
# PORTAL_PASSCODE=
# PORTAL_ADMIN_PASSCODE=
# PORTAL_SECRET=
#
# Single-tenant deployments: confine the client login to ONE workspace. Without
# it a signed-in client can see the whole client roster at "/" — who else Pexalo
# works with and what they bought. The Pexalo login still sees everything.
# PORTAL_CLIENT_REF=coinpresso

# Re-billing markup shown on the API costs page to the Pexalo login only.
# BILLING_MARKUP_PCT=10
# Flat monthly hosting allowance added to the billable figure (not marked up).
# 0 or unset = hosting is included in the retainer and no tile is shown.
# BILLING_HOSTING_USD=0
